  "instance_name": "honor_killings",
  "label": "Honor Killings",
  "description": "A real-world social and legal phenomenon in which individuals, often women or girls, are murdered by family members or close relatives because they are perceived to have brought dishonor to the family. This practice is rooted in patriarchal norms and is prevalent in some cultures, particularly in parts of South Asia, the Middle East, and elsewhere, though it is not universally accepted or practiced. The term 'honor killing' is often used to describe acts of violence justified by the perpetrator as necessary to restore or preserve family honor.",
